    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθοσμ-ίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>redolent of flowers,</i> almost always of wine, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος ἀ.</span>”
				<i>with a fine bouquet,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Steril.</u>
					235
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				807
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1150
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				108.30
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				6.2.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sat.</u>
				22
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				2
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. λειμῶνες,</span> as a pedantic
			phrase:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθόσμ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1150
			</span></i>.</div>
